	(text "Front end: S12023-10 APD, OPA857 TIA, AC coupling, VCA821 VGA, level shift to SDET. Left to right in signal order."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c90e0613-a5fc-4084-9174-e81dcdac0736")
	)
	(text "HV: HV_K is the APD cathode net (up to 220 V). Keep-out from TIA_IN (200 V creepage/clearance). No HV test points. R50 and C50 sit at the cathode."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f0a75301-3878-41b4-9581-258bb713c9e6")
	)
	(text "APD polarity: cathode (D10 pin 1) to positive bias, anode (pin 3) to TIA_IN, case (pin 2) to GND. D11 FDS010 is a DNP bench fallback on the same nets."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cbeb6254-895f-46d2-9fd5-2d4c2a576b40")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A, nothing here is simulated or measured)\nPROPOSED   Stage 2 filter R50 10k (1206, 200 V) + C50 10n (1210, 500 V C0G) at the cathode from APD_BIAS to HV_K; stage 1 is on the Power sheet. 2 uC dump-risk note and 4.7n alternative: open test item.\nVERIFIED   Polarity and pins: S12023-10 K=1, CASE=2, A=3 (lab library symbol). Cathode to positive bias (standing correction 2). 6 pF for S12023-10 and FDS010 alike.\nVERIFIED   OPA857: Test_SD (13) to GND and Test_IN (14) to +VS for normal operation (SBOS630D p.4 pin table); CTRL logic 1 = 20k, 0 = 5k, VIH 2 V, VIL 0.8 V (p.6-7); OUTN is a 1.83 V typ reference (p.6, VICR).\nPROPOSED   JP10 3-pad solder jumper on CTRL: common = CTRL, default bridge to the 3V3 side (20k gain), GND side = 5k. Footprint is open, bridge at assembly.\nPROPOSED   OPA857 VS+ (9, 10, 11) on 3V3 with 2 x 100n 0402 + 1u 0603; all GND pins and PAD to GND; NC (16) no connect. Keep decouplers < 0.25 in from the pins (p.24 layout).\nPROPOSED   AC coupling C51/C52 100n into R51/R52 10k to GND (corner 159 Hz); both OUT and OUTN coupled (standing correction 1).\nVERIFIED   VCA821 DGS pins and RF 402 / RG 80.6 for 20 dB (SBOS407D p.4 pin table, p.28 Table 2: RG 80, RF 402 is the G = 10 column). RF is compensation (standing correction 5): keep the datasheet network.\nPROPOSED   VG through R55 100 + C53 1n. VCC pins on +/-3V7 with 100n 0402 + 2u2 0603 each.\nUNRESOLVED Datasheet input limit (p.9, Figure: VIN max = 2 x RG x 2.6 mA) is ~0.42 Vpp at RG = 80 ohm; the 20k TIA path saturates it near 21 uA peak. RG may need to move up.\nUNRESOLVED OPA857 stability at 6 pF source capacitance is not verified. The datasheet characterises CS = 1.5 pF (p.6).\nPROPOSED   Level shift C54 10n + R56 10k to VCM_DET (corner 1.6 kHz). TP10 VGA_OUT, TP11 SDET, TP12 TIA_REF.\nUNRESOLVED VCA821 supply is specified 7 V to 12 V total (p.36); +/-3.7 V is 7.4 V, 0.4 V above the minimum."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 175 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5cde7f11-eef0-449a-a691-6d0da47e169a")
	)
